From 8fb4fb64dffc0b834cff871eb7dfba6f9058260b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: desocketed <desocketed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:28:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] vk_exec: NX2NAVI_AO_ORDER=1 runs the ambient occlusion
 again after the event it waits for, inside the signalling submission's replay
 (default 0) (#146)

The worker queues wait (WaitEvent) for the main submission's signal that the
half-resolution depth is written, then compute the occlusion; replayed in
submission order the occlusion read the previous frame's depth, so it trails
one frame behind anything that moves on screen. The replay now notes each
unmet wait with the queue state there and, at the matching signal op, replays
the binds and the occlusion dispatches (occlusion, two blurs) recorded after
the wait once more, then returns to the signalling submission. Nothing is cut
or held, fences are unchanged; the waiting recording is kept alive 64 submits.
Asynchronous replay only.

Lab, nx2navi.ao: 300 of 300 frames read this frame's depth (before: 0);
standing still at the castle slot and the graveyard no brightness outliers in
300 frames either way, sharpness and frame rate unchanged (28.2 vs 28.4 and
33.1-33.4 vs 33.2-33.8 fps), crash spot frame 1700 passes. Event waits v3 on
the same castle spot: the region 23% darker with 5 dark frames in 300.
